    "turn_text": "But what she does do is make sure the state has a lot of free labor. This was Tulsi Gabbard's point. That Kamala Harris, as the Attorney General, kept people in jail for longer than they should have been, so the state had more free labor. But I'm hearing from Elizabeth Warren, a host of others, Trump is afraid of strong women. This argument is just joyous as it is madness. Tony Katz, 93 W I B C. Good morning. Good to be with you. Joe Biden has decided not to run for reelection, or at least that's what we're told. And when I say that's what we're told, I mean we haven't heard from him. All we have is a statement. That's it. We have not heard from him. We have not seen video of him. Nothing. Always said is it's best that I focus on the remainder of my term. Then he puts out a second statement on social media endorsing Kamala Harris. Interesting that he did both on X formerly Twitter because and this was pointed out well on social media That here is Twitter and Elon must buys it and changes the name to X And now it's just a platform for white supremacists and bigots and that's where Joe Biden goes to announce. He's not running for reelection Weird arguments these people make very very weird Meanwhile, will it be Harris, Kamala Harris, the Vice President by default? Will there be an open primary? Joe Manchin says he will not be a candidate. He wants to see an either an open primary or a mini primary. I don't know how you do either one of these things. No clue how you get this done. Closer to home, very happy to see it. The NIT, right? When you don't make it to the NCAA, we don't make it to the dance. You end up in the NIT, the National Invitation Tournament. They're gonna be holding the semifinals and the championship at Hinkle Field House for the second straight year. That is fantastic, fantastic news. Indianapolis is going to host the NIT semifinal and final in 2026, along with the division 1, 2, and 3 men's titles games. That's in 2026, everything, all basketball is in Indiana and rightfully so. This is pretty solid. I think this is great, right? Okay, I get it. People don't pay as much attention to the NIT. You don't want to have to go to the NIT tournament, but If you're gonna have a championship, you're gonna bring some bucks, you're gonna bring it. Why not have it here? I think it's great. Good on Butler, smart for Hinkle. Sell it out. Fantastic stuff. Joe Biden out of the race, of course that is the top story and it has a series of ramifications. Congressman Jim Banks scheduled to be with us and Andrew Horning is the Libertarian candidate for Senate. He will be with us on Friday. I was supposed to schedule it today because of Joe Biden getting out of the race, things move around. So I want to thank him for being okay with moving to Friday because I'll be out for a few days in D.C. for the Netanyahu speech. We will absolutely speak to him and it won't be the last time the Libertarian candidate for Senate joins us on Friday. Be sure to tune in then Tony Katz, 93 W.I.B.C. Good morning.",
