    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/6/86263.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 10,
    "turn_text": "Yeah, the whole thing is weird, Tony. I mean, presidents don't take vacations. They don't take days off. They're always on. They're expected to be on because at any given moment, you don't know what's going to happen. That's going to require the attention of a president and this president is missing. I mean, I The announcement came yesterday. You make a good point. When LBJ made that announcement, he appeared before the American people and made that announcement. You know, this is unprecedented, but that's the best comparison. LBJ in March of an election year saying that he's dropping out of the race and he won't be the Democrat Party nominee. This is late July. The president does it by social media. It doesn't appear before the people. And then he scrubs his entire public schedule. He's got nothing on his schedule today. And that's the part of it that should be concerning to the American people. It's not just that if he can't run again, he shouldn't be president. It's that this guy is clearly incapable of performing the duties of the president, the United States and commander in chief of this country. And there's an expectation that he's going to do it for another six months. That to me, that's scary. Knowing what's going on around the world, the issues around the with the hot spots around the world this this guy is not capable of leading this country for another six months and he should resign because of it",
